Calculate the intersection of a rectangle and line segment.

This function is used to clip a line segment to a rectangle. A line segment contained entirely within the rectangle or that does not intersect will remain unchanged. A line segment that crosses the rectangle at either or both ends will be clipped to the boundary of the rectangle and the new coordinates saved in `X1`, `Y1`, `X2`, and/or `Y2` as necessary.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item rect - SDL3::Rect object or undef. an SDL_Rect structure representing the rectangle to intersect.

=item X1 - reference to a scalar holding integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer to the starting X-coordinate of the line.

=item Y1 - reference to a scalar holding integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer to the starting Y-coordinate of the line.

=item X2 - reference to a scalar holding integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer to the ending X-coordinate of the line.

=item Y2 - reference to a scalar holding integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer to the ending Y-coordinate of the line.

=back

Returns boolean: true if there is an intersection, false otherwise.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

